Only same-origin HTTPS candidates with explicit document roles are proposed. URLs with credentials, private literal IPs, unsupported schemes, malformed ports or local-style hosts are rejected. External legitimate CDNs remain deferred by this narrow prototype. HTTP fragment removal is request deduplication only; version-bearing paths/query parameters remain unchanged and no section/full-document identity is asserted. One hop, one candidate, cycle/dedup checks; no website fallback or recursive traversal.

